sequenceDiagram
    participant Kubelet as Kubelet<br/>(Health Checks)
    participant User as Platform Admin
    participant KubeAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant Controller as feast-operator<br/>controller-manager
    participant FeastOp as Upstream Feast<br/>Operator
    participant Prometheus as Prometheus<br/>(monitoring.coreos.com)

    Note over Controller: Startup
    Controller->>KubeAPI: Register watches<br/>ServiceAccount Token Auth
    KubeAPI-->>Controller: Watch streams established

    Note over Kubelet,Controller: Health & Readiness Probes
    Kubelet->>Controller: GET /healthz :8081<br/>HTTP (no auth)
    Controller-->>Kubelet: 200 OK
    Kubelet->>Controller: GET /readyz :8081<br/>HTTP (no auth)
    Controller-->>Kubelet: 200 OK

    Note over User,Controller: FeastOperator CR Lifecycle
    User->>KubeAPI: Create FeastOperator CR<br/>(cluster-scoped, name=default-feastoperator)
    KubeAPI-->>Controller: Watch event: FeastOperator created
    Controller->>KubeAPI: Create Deployment<br/>(upstream Feast operator)
    Controller->>KubeAPI: Create ServiceAccount, RBAC
    Controller->>KubeAPI: Create ConfigMaps
    Controller->>KubeAPI: Create Services
    Controller->>KubeAPI: Create ServiceMonitor
    Controller->>KubeAPI: Create Routes (OpenShift)
    Controller->>KubeAPI: Update FeastOperator status

    Note over FeastOp,KubeAPI: Upstream Feast Operator Reconciliation
    FeastOp->>KubeAPI: Watch FeatureStore CRs<br/>(namespaced)
    KubeAPI-->>FeastOp: FeatureStore events
    FeastOp->>KubeAPI: Create Deployments, Services,<br/>CronJobs, HPAs, PDBs, PVCs

    Note over Prometheus,Controller: Metrics Collection
    Prometheus->>Controller: GET /metrics :8443<br/>RBAC (TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview)
    Controller-->>Prometheus: Prometheus metrics
